The upstream replan FSM hard-codes the formation-centre height to 0.5 m and
ignores the z of the goal it was given.

A 0.5 m centre does not survive the qn plant's vertical transient: measured on
two runs the lowest member reaches about 0.237 m within half a second of the
first dispatch, independent of the reference speed, so the declared 0.25 m
platform envelope crosses the z=0 surface.  The height therefore has to be a
scenario parameter that the caller can raise, and the goal message already
carries it.

The upstream file is not modified in the repository; this patch is applied at
image build time and is recorded here.

--- a/src/planner/plan_manage/src/ego_replan_fsm.cpp
+++ b/src/planner/plan_manage/src/ego_replan_fsm.cpp
@@ -639,7 +639,12 @@
     bool success = false;
     swarm_central_pos_(0) = msg->pose.position.x;
     swarm_central_pos_(1) = msg->pose.position.y;
-    swarm_central_pos_(2) = 0.5;
+    // Honour the requested formation-centre height instead of hard-coding it.
+    // The qn plant's vertical transient at task start reaches about 0.26 m below
+    // the cruise altitude, so a 0.5 m centre leaves the declared 0.25 m platform
+    // envelope below the z=0 surface; the height therefore has to be a scenario
+    // parameter rather than a constant.  See docs/QN_INTEGRATION.md.
+    swarm_central_pos_(2) = msg->pose.position.z;
 
     int id = planner_manager_->pp_.drone_id;
 
